n on a draw or have a marginal hand. Betting here risks turning my hand into a bluff against Aces.\n\nReason:\nGiven that I have one pair of Kings with a weak kicker (9), and an Ace appeared on the river, this is a dangerous spot to continue betting. My opponent has called two streets of aggression but hasn't raised, suggesting either a drawing hand or a marginal made hand. With the Ace on the river, there's a significant chance they either:\n1. Made a pair of Aces (which beats me)\n2. Already had Aces and were slow-playing\n3. Missed their draw\n\nSince I've already built a decent pot with my previous bets, checking here is the most prudent play. It allows me to get to showdown without risking more chips in a spot where I'm likely either slightly ahead or behind. Betting would primarily get called by hands that beat me (any Ace) and get folds from hands I'm already beating.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
